[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660122492","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102834#issuecomment-2660122492","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102834","id":2660122492,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ejj98","user":{"login":"suddjian","id":1858430,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NTg0MzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1858430?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian","html_url":"https://github.com/suddjian","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-14T19:37:16Z","updated_at":"2025-02-16T21:58:05Z","body":"> Note that when you drag an item away from an expanded folder, it won't collapse again (even after releasing the mouse). Ideally, I'd prefer the previous folding state to be restored after releasing the mouse, with the exception of the folder the resource was dropped in.\r\nThis prevents situations where you end up with a lot of expanded folders because you were hesitating about the target folder.\r\n\r\nI considered doing this, but I haven't encountered a tree interface that behaves this way. Is it really user-expected behavior? I personally think that a user merely considering dropping into a tree branch is a meaningful enough interaction to keep that branch open until they decide to close it, but open to other opinions.\r\n\r\nThe inspector's drag-unfolding also doesn't undo on exit. Just to note that the precedent is to not re-fold, and if this is added, the inspector should do it as well.\r\n\r\nI anticipate some tricky edge cases with this, since drag-unfolded tree items could change state independently from the drag events, but I think I can do it. Do you consider re-folding-on-exit a requirement for getting this accepted? Maybe it would be better as a second PR?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660122492/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661158205","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102834#issuecomment-2661158205","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102834","id":2661158205,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eng09","user":{"login":"suddjian","id":1858430,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NTg0MzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1858430?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian","html_url":"https://github.com/suddjian","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suddjian/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_ad